Osiris the firstborn son of Gabe a newt  Osiris was considered the king of the  underworld and a prominent figure in  Egyptian mythology Osiris is not always  considered a god many of the ancient  texts believe that Osiris was once human  murdered by his brother Seth Seth was  jealous of Osiris his power and  popularity and lusted after his wife  Osiris was married to his sister Isis a  custom that was common amongst most  Pharaohs as a God could only marry a  goddess Osiris made his wife the regent  of Egypt instead of set this was the  last straw for set he decided that he  would kill Osiris and take the power he  believed to be rightfully his  he held a banquet in the name of Osiris  and made the cedarwood  evany chest for the occasion he offered  the chest to anyone who could fit into  it however the chest was made to fit for  Osiris himself as he planned  no one could fit into the chest and the  last person to try was Osiris when he  laid down in the chest set slammed on  the lid and nailed it down he sealed it  with molten lead and threw it in the  River Nile the chest  eventually re-emerged this angered set  he tore his brother's corpse into 14  pieces and scattered them all throughout  Egypt once all the pieces of Osiris were  found and buried he was reborn as the  ruler and judge of the underworld  it is believed that Anubis who had reign  over the underworld at the time stepped  aside out of respect for Cyrus  of cyrus was considered a good and  honorable leader during his lifetime and  his presence in the underworld no doubt  gave people comfort he is usually seen  as a just generous and giving God  however there are some depictions of him  as a terrifying figure who would  dispatch his demon messengers to drag  the living to the realm of the dead  Osiris commonly appeared as a mummified  King he skin green or black to represent  the fact that he is dead he often has a  curved ceremonial beard a crown and he  signature flail his crown is usually  white sometimes with the plume of  feathers which are thought to represent  the cult of Osiris Osiris was also  considered the god of fertility in  agriculture he was able to grant life  from the underworld from sprouting  vegetation to the annual flood of the  River Nile  some argue that Osiris was a symbol of  resurrection and others saw him as  signifying the renewal of life in the  next world after the rule Osiris did not  rise from the dead there are rumors that  believe the ancient Egyptians were  cannibals until Osiris developed  agriculture and persuaded them to stop  there is no definitive evidence that the  ancient Egyptians were cannibals but the  legends state that Osiris brought order  to Egypt and established culture and  stability amongst the people it is  believed that Egypt was plunged into  chaos when Osiris was murdered only when  Osiris his son Horus defeated set and  took back the throne was harmony  restored  if you've enjoyed this video then please  go ahead and leave it a like consider  subscribing if folklore mythology is  something that interests you  if you have anything you'd like to  discuss or have any ideas for future  videos then please go ahead and let me  know in the comments below as always  I've been your host mythology and  folklore explained
 

